        {
          "text": "HSIEH Chang-t'ing 謝章鋌 (T. 枚如, H. 樂階退叟), Dec. 28, 1820–1903, poet, scholar, essayist, was a native of Ch'ang-lo, Fukien, a descendant of a literary family. He was sickly as a child. His mother died when he was two years old, and he was brought up by his stepmother.",
